WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.167
-Hi, hi, hi, hi, hi. -Welcome back to the show.

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:04.400
It is so great to see you.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.801
-I haven't seen you since, like, the pandemic.

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:06.934
-I know. -That was a thing.

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.400
-We have a -- That was totally a thing.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.801
I have so many questions. -Okay.

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:11.901
-First of all, I know you're an Eagles fan.

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:14.300
-Well, I'm a Patriots fan. I'm from Massachusetts.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.234
But my side chick is the Eagles 'cause I went to school

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:18.133
in Philly and my husband is a Philly fan.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:20.200
-Oh. -Yes.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.000
-Your side piece?

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.400
-My side piece are the Iggles, yeah, yeah.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.133
-Yeah, yeah. And where did you watch the game?

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:30.400
-Well, unfortunately, I was on the airplane coming here.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.968
-Oh. -And the first half was great.

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:35.167
I felt really good about the first half actually.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:37.534
-Oh, yeah. -And then we were coming in

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:39.968
for a landing, like, right as we were counting down

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.000
to the halftime, and I was like, "God dang it.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.400
This plane is going to land

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.868
right as Rihanna is coming out on stage."

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:49.133
And, Jimmy, a Rihanna miracle happened!

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:51.267
We landed -- -Delay.

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:53.767
-"Your gate is -- There's a plane at the gate."

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:54.968
-Yeah. The gate took off.

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:56.467
-"We got to sit here for 15 minutes."

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.534
-The gate left. The gate is in Pittsburgh.

00:00:58.534 --> 00:01:00.634
-And it was, like, we just -- we got to sit here for 15 minutes,

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:02.934
and I got to watch the whole Rihanna halftime show.

00:01:02.934 --> 00:01:04.834
-Yeah! So it worked out okay.

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:06.701
-It was a Rihanna miracle. Yeah. -And then you unboarded.

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:08.234
And then you didn't see the end.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.567
-I missed -- No, I saw the end in the hotel last night.

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:12.167
-Oh. -And, yeah, that wasn't great.

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:13.767
-Yeah. But you're here tonight. And thank you --

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:15.300
-I mean, congrats to the Chiefs, by the way.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.100
-Yeah, congrats to the Chiefs. -Congrats to the Chiefs.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.000
-Thank you for coming all the way here and doing our show.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.200
We appreciate this. It's also kicking off Perm Week.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.534
-Ah, yeah. -It's a big deal.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:23.701
Everyone's talking about it.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:24.968
-By the way, that guy -- He looks amazing!

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.634
-He looks fantastic, right? Yeah.

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:28.434
But I asked you if you ever had a perm.

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:29.801
-Ugh. Yeah.

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:31.734
-And you were nice enough to give us this photo.

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:33.334
You did have a perm.

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:35.267
-Well, technically -- So, what's amazing is --

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:36.467
-Everyone went, "Oh."

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:37.767
-Yeah. -How cute.

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:39.200
-You guys didn't think that I was really

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.400
gonna show up with that.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.701
That's actually just my natural hair, Jimmy.

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:44.901
-Is it really? -Yeah. I didn't even perm that.

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:48.968
I thought that if I got a perm that I would get, like,

00:01:48.968 --> 00:01:52.868
I don't know, like, beautiful model curls or something.

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:55.133
-Yeah. -And so I did a perm

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:58.100
on top of that -- on top of that hair.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.868
-How can you perm this hair? -Correct.

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:01.934
It's -- What ended up happening is --

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:03.100
-It straightened it.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.300
-It shrunk onto my head into little curls

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:06.634
and I looked like my Grammy.

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:08.434
-Aww. See?

00:02:08.434 --> 00:02:10.801
-Like, she went every week and had, like, her little perm done.

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:13.400
And that's -- Yeah, there's not a lot of photos of that.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.667
I refused to get that photographed.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.534
-Did this little girl ever think she's going to go on

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:19.167
to act and direct and -- -First of all,

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:21.701
this little girl, when this photo was taken,

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:24.968
that it would be shown on the effing "Tonight Show"

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:27.033
is crazy to me!

00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:29.100
-Come on. Isn't that cool? -Come on!

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.501
-Come on, bud. -That girl had no idea.

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:33.367
-Look at what you're doing. -I don't know.

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:34.901
-I want to talk about your movie.

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:36.534
Let me just tell you something. This came out.

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:38.767
I go -- "Cocaine Bear" is trending on Twitter.

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:41.267
I go, "What in the world is 'Cocaine Bear'"?

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:43.534
The trailer for your movie.

00:02:43.534 --> 00:02:44.767
-Yeah. -Exploded.

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:45.934
Number-one trend on Twitter.

00:02:45.934 --> 00:02:47.601
Everyone's talking about this amazing trailer.

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:49.200
The movie is hilarious. -Thank you.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.868
-It's based on a semi-true story.

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:53.334
-Inspired by a true story. -Inspired by a true story.

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:54.767
-Yes, yes. -Gosh, it's funny, by the way.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:57.067
-Thank you so much. Yeah, it's a true story.

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:59.868
There was a drug runner in the 1980s,

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:02.667
and his M.O. was that he would drop drugs

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:06.567
out of a low-flying plane for people to pick up on the ground.

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:08.701
And this one night, the drug run goes wrong.

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:10.834
He drops the drugs into the woods,

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:12.300
and a bear gets into the drugs.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.901
This all happened in real life. -Yeah.

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:16.100
-And they never recovered any of the drugs.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.234
But what they found months later

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:21.701
was an OD'd bear in the woods... -Yeah.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.734
-...who had eaten, like, 70 pounds of cocaine.

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:27.067
And so this movie imagines what would have happened

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:30.133
in the hours after that bear first found the bag.

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:31.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:36.300
-So it's a bear -- it's a bear on a cocaine bender.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.734
-It's a bear on a bender. -A bear on cocaine.

00:03:38.734 --> 00:03:40.534
-Yeah. -It's insanity.

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:43.667
It is complete insanity what happens.

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:47.434
People hiking in the woods, and they meet up with Cocaine Bear.

00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:50.901
It's a -- The CGI is amazing. -Thank you.

00:03:50.901 --> 00:03:52.501
-I'm assuming a lot of it's --

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:53.834
-It's all -- There was no real bear.

00:03:53.834 --> 00:03:55.100
-Yeah. -But I get asked a lot about

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:56.501
what it was like to work with a real bear.

00:03:56.501 --> 00:03:58.200
And I really am proud of that.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:01.234
Because that was the goal, to create a photorealistic --

00:04:01.234 --> 00:04:03.334
-You did a great job. -I wanted it to seem like

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:05.868
it was a documentary, Jimmy, of a bear...

00:04:05.868 --> 00:04:07.634
-Yeah. --...doing cocaine, you know?

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:10.067
-I love how much money went into this "Cocaine Bear."

00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:12.901
-I mean, it's like a Marvel movie, but a giant Cocaine Bear.

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:14.334
Yeah. -Truly. Truly.

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:16.267
-This is -- You brought -- You were nice enough to bring

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:17.501
a behind-the-scenes -- -Oh, yeah.

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:18.968
-One of the actors? -That's Allan Henry.

00:04:18.968 --> 00:04:20.434
He's our bear performer.

00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:23.734
So, this guy trained under Andy Serkis,

00:04:23.734 --> 00:04:25.400
who did "Planet of the Apes."

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.968
He walks as a quadruped on all fours

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:29.100
on these, like, special -- Like, anybody would --

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.734
You'd blow your back out in two seconds.

00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:32.334
-Oh, of course. -It takes a lot of training

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:34.000
to actually be able to do this work.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.267
This is -- You know, so, those are the fake eyes

00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:38.033
and the eyeline and everything for the actors.

00:04:38.033 --> 00:04:39.601
-So the actors would see that... -Exactly.

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:41.133
-So we would all -- -...coming after them.

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:42.567
-We would see that -- coming after them.

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:43.767
He's a stunt performer, as well,

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:45.767
so he can really attack and throw people around.

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:47.834
You've seen the movie. Things happen.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:50.934
-Things happen in the first 30 seconds of this movie.

00:04:50.934 --> 00:04:52.567
Oh, here's another.

00:04:52.567 --> 00:04:55.133
This one is actually just a fake real head.

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:56.701
-Well, so, this head -- That's our real --

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:58.400
That is what our bear looks like.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.234
Cokie. We call the bear Cokie.

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:03.067
And Cokie -- -Cokie the Bear.

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:04.834
-Cokie. -Of course, Cokie, yeah.

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:07.334
-So, Cokie -- These nice gentlemen

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:09.467
would sort of walk around with Cokie

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:10.968
as, like, a lighting reference.

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:12.901
And now that head is in my house.

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:14.701
It's in my office. -Wow.

00:05:14.701 --> 00:05:17.901
-And recently a repair guy came over and walked in there,

00:05:17.901 --> 00:05:19.400
turned the light on, and lost his mind.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:20.734
-He's like, "Aah!

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:22.901
You got to tell me if there's a bear head in here."

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:25.300
-Came in. He's like, "That really -- What is that thing?"

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:26.567
"Oh." -Yeah, it's Cokie.

00:05:26.567 --> 00:05:27.834
-"We made this movie. That's Cokie."

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:29.400
-"We made a movie called 'Cocaine Bear.'" Yeah.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.133
I want to show a clip.

00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:33.501
Here's a look at a scene from "Cocaine Bear."

00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:35.000
Check this out.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.801
-[ Panting ]

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:38.234
Where is it?!

00:05:38.234 --> 00:05:40.067
♪♪

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:41.434
-Hey!

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:43.767
-[ Grunting ]

00:05:43.767 --> 00:05:45.267
-What should I do?!

00:05:45.267 --> 00:05:48.300
♪♪

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.000
-Ohh!

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.634
Aah! Oh, oh, oh!

00:05:53.634 --> 00:05:56.467
Ohh. There's something wrong with it.

00:05:56.467 --> 00:05:57.968
-Yeah, I told you there was.

00:05:57.968 --> 00:06:00.300
-Why is it acting like this?

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:02.367
Did you feed it cocaine?!

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:04.834
-No. But you're safe.

00:06:04.834 --> 00:06:06.334
Bears can't climb trees.

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:08.434
-Of course they can!

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.267
-Then why are you up here?

00:06:10.267 --> 00:06:12.934
♪♪

00:06:12.934 --> 00:06:14.901
-[ Whimpering ]

00:06:14.901 --> 00:06:16.767
-Elizabeth Banks, everyone.

00:06:16.767 --> 00:06:21.100
"Cocaine Bear" is in theaters February 24th.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:23.067
Kelsey Grammer joins us after the break.

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:24.300
Stick around, everybody.

